Node-assertable surface — the honest walk-gated verdict
-------------------------------------------------------
Nothing in this diff is node-assertable, and this is stated plainly (never fabricated):

  - The change is pure CSS in app.css. The Vitest suite renders component MARKUP
    (JSDOM / react-dom static markup) and asserts on class names, element counts,
    and rendered text — it does NOT load app.css or read computed styles. There is
    no CSS-property assertion surface in the suite to add to.
  - The design (brainstorm.md v3, Test plan sketch + Assumptions ledger) predicts
    exactly this: "Zero new node tests expected (pure CSS phase; grouped selectors).
    Any churned literal pin enumerated (expected zero — no markup change)."
  - Therefore no new node test is added. The visual result (schedule type, panel
    dress, SVG label font, foundation stroke weight, focus-visible ring) is verified
    by the manual both-media walk, recorded below as a checklist — not by an assertion.

