Drift hunt (pre-implementation, against live worktree source)
-------------------------------------------------------------
  - Six container classes exact & present: link-inspector (LinkInspector.tsx:160),
    findings-panel (FindingsPanel.tsx:138/152/163), summary-cards (SummaryCards.tsx:19),
    plans-bar (PlansBar.tsx:56), chain-builder (ChainBuilder.tsx:98),
    alt-compare (AltCompare.tsx:133).
  - Two real tables only: train-table (LinkInspector.tsx thead/tr/th),
    alt-compare-table (AltCompare.tsx:137, thead/tr/th). ChainBuilder preview is a
    <ul class="chain-builder-rows"> (ChainBuilder.tsx:135) — a list, not a table.
  - All 8 SVG label classes present in source: lane-name, machine-label,
    bp-machine-label, bp-lane-name, bp-mark-label, chain-bp-name, chain-bp-power,
    chain-bp-link-label.
  - Foundation: .bp-foundation is SHARED by the schematic-blueprint and the
    combined-chain blueprint (ChainBlueprint.tsx:183 renders className="bp-foundation";
    app.css:605 keys .chain-bp-site.selected .bp-foundation). There is NO separate
    chain-bp-foundation class — so the design's "bp-foundation and the chain-bp
    equivalent" collapses to ONE selector (.bp-foundation) that covers both views.
    This is a simplification, not drift: intent (both foundations to --border-soft)
    is fully met by the single selector.
  - Panel headers: only TWO panels carry a title/header element —
    .link-inspector-title (LinkInspector.tsx:162) and .alt-compare-head
    (AltCompare.tsx:134). SummaryCards, PlansBar, ChainBuilder, FindingsPanel are
    control bars / lists with no heading element. The label idiom is applied to the
    two header classes that exist ("the existing header classes per panel").
  - No :focus rule exists in app.css today (grep confirmed) — the a11y premise holds;
    the new :focus-visible rule is disjoint from the .selected canvas outline idioms.
  - No new tokens: every value maps to an existing token (--font-mono-num, --fg,
    --border-soft, --accent, --bg-panel, --fg-muted).

